      "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=x+\\tan\\left(\\frac{1}{2}x\\right)\\qquad\\pi&lt;x&lt;\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Given that the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=0\"></span> has a single root <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> lies in the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[3.6,3.7]\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f^{\\prime}(x)\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Using 3.7 as a first approximation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>, apply the Newton–Raphson method once to obtain a second approximation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>. Give your answer to 3 decimal places. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
