    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2024-june/q5",
      "question": "<p>The function f is defined by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{2x-3}{x^2+4}\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb R\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f&#x27;(x)=\\frac{ax^2+bx+c}{\\left(x^2+4\\right)^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> are constants to be found.</p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Hence, using algebra, find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> for which f is decreasing.<p>You must show each step in your working.</p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
