      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2024-june/q6",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:90mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-2024-june/q06-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1. V-shaped graph with vertex P above the positive x-axis, slightly to the right of the y-axis; the left branch crosses the positive y-axis.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows a sketch of the graph with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=3|x-2|+5\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The vertex of the graph is at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>, shown in Figure 1.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Solve the equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"16-4x=3|x-2|+5\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>A line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=kx+4\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> intersects <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3|x-2|+5\"></span> at 2 distinct points,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>find the range of values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
