      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2024-june/q7",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:100mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-2024-june/q07-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. A cylindrical tank of height 1.5 m, partly filled with water to depth H m, with a small hole at point L in its side above the water surface. Diagram not drawn to scale.\"></figure><p>Figure 2 shows a cylindrical tank of height <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.5\\,\\mathrm m\"></span>.</p><p>Initially the tank is full of water.</p><p>The water starts to leak from a small hole, at a point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"L\"></span>, in the side of the tank.</p><p>While the tank is leaking, the depth, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"H\"></span> metres, of the water in the tank is modelled by the differential equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm dH}{\\mathrm dt}=-0.12\\mathrm e^{-0.2t}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> hours is the time after the leak starts.</p><p>Using the model,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"H=A\\mathrm e^{-0.2t}+B\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are constants to be found,</p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>find the time taken for the depth of the water to decrease to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.2\\,\\mathrm m\"></span>. Give your answer in hours and minutes, to the nearest minute. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>In the long term, the water level in the tank falls to the same height as the hole.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>Find, according to the model, the height of the hole from the bottom of the tank. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
