      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2024-june/q8",
      "question": "<p>The functions f and g are defined by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=4-3x^2\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb R\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g(x)=\\frac{5}{2x-9}\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb R,\\ x\\neq\\frac{9}{2}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{fg}(2)\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g^{-1}\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{gf}(x)\"></span>, giving your answer as a simplified fraction.</li><li>Deduce the range of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{gf}(x)\"></span>.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>The function h is defined by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm h(x)=2x^2-6x+k\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb R\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li>Find the range of values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> for which the equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\mathrm h(x)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>has no real solutions.</p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
