      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:130mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-2024-june/q10-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 3. Curve y = 8x - x^(5/2) for x &gt;= 0 rising from O to a maximum and crossing the x-axis at A. Line l2 through O and line l1, the tangent at A, meet above the curve; region R between the two lines and the curve is shaded.\"></figure><p><strong>In this question you must show all stages of your working.</strong></p><p><strong>Solutions relying entirely on calculator technology are not acceptable.</strong></p><p>Figure 3 shows a sketch of part of the curve with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=8x-x^{\\frac{5}{2}}\\qquad x\\geqslant0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The curve crosses the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Verify that the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> coordinate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is 4 <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> is the tangent to the curve at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Use calculus to show that an equation of line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> is<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"12x+y=48\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=8x\"></span></p><p>The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 3, is bounded by the curve, the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>Use algebraic integration to find the exact area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol>",
