      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2024-june/q12",
      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\"><li>Express <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"140\\cos\\theta-480\\sin\\theta\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"K\\cos(\\theta+\\alpha)\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"K&gt;0\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;\\alpha&lt;90^\\circ\"></span></p><p>State the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"K\"></span> and give the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>, in degrees, to 2 decimal places.</p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>A scientist studies the number of rabbits and the number of foxes in a wood for one year.</p><p>The number of rabbits, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"R=A+140\\cos(30t)^\\circ-480\\sin(30t)^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> months is the time after the start of the year and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>Given that, during the year, the maximum number of rabbits in the wood is 1500</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>find a complete equation for this model.</li><li>Hence write down the minimum number of rabbits in the wood during the year according to the model.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The actual number of rabbits in the wood is at its minimum value in the middle of April.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>Use this information to comment on the model for the number of rabbits. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The number of foxes, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F\"></span>, in the wood during the same year is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"F=100+70\\sin(30t+70)^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The number of foxes is at its minimum value after <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> months.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li>Find, according to the models, the number of <strong>rabbits</strong> in the wood at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> months. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
