      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\"><li>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> is a positive constant, use the substitution <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=a\\sin^2\\theta\"></span> to show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int_0^a x^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\sqrt{a-x}\\,\\mathrm dx=\\frac{1}{2}a^2\\int_0^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\sin^22\\theta\\,\\mathrm d\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Hence use algebraic integration to show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int_0^a x^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\sqrt{a-x}\\,\\mathrm dx=k\\pi a^2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant to be found.</p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
