      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2024-june/q14",
      "question": "<p>A balloon is being inflated.</p><p>In a simple model,</p><ul><li>the balloon is modelled as a sphere</li><li>the rate of increase of the radius of the balloon is inversely proportional to the square root of the radius of the balloon</li></ul><p>At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> seconds, the radius of the balloon is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\\,\\mathrm{cm}\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Write down a differential equation to model this situation. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>At the instant when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=10\"></span></p><ul><li>the radius is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"16\\,\\mathrm{cm}\"></span></li><li>the radius is increasing at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.9\\,\\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}\"></span></li></ul><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Solve the differential equation to show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r^{\\frac{3}{2}}=5.4t+10\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>Hence find the radius of the balloon when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=20\"></span><p>Give your answer to the nearest millimetre.</p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Suggest a limitation of the model. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
